.	http://purl.oclc.org/NET/cmcs/schema/:hasConfigurations		<rdf:Bag xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" > <rdf:li><rdf:href xlink:href="Parameters/chemsys.mvm" xlink:type="simple"></rdf:href></rdf:li></rdf:Bag>
.	http://www.emsl.pnl.gov/ecce:annotation		Quantum ESPRESSO, PBE-D3(BJ), plane waves (60 Ry), 4x4x4 k-points, atoms relaxed in the fixed cell. This calculation shows a molecular crystal of linear CO2 molecules with no hydrogen bonds, held together only by weak dispersion forces, which is why dry ice sublimes so easily. Structure: CO2 (Pa-3, 150 K), COD 9007643.
.	http://www.emsl.pnl.gov/ecce:application		QuantumESPRESSO
